# ==============================================================================
# Detection: Multiple Failed Windows Network Logons (DET-01)
# Canonical Source: detections/sigma/windows_failed_logon.yml
# Target Platform: Splunk Enterprise / Splunk Cloud
# MITRE ATT&CK: T1110.001 (Credential Access: Password Guessing)
# ==============================================================================
#
# ARCHITECTURAL TRANSLATION MAPPING:
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Sigma Intent:
#    Detect Event 4625 records with LogonType=3 and bad password status codes
#    aggregated by target account and source IP over a 5-minute sliding window.
#
# 2. Splunk Implementation:
#    Uses streamstats with time_window=5m to maintain a sliding aggregation
#    window across events, filtering where failure_count >= 5.
#
# 3. Semantic Differences from Sigma:
#    - Splunk field names: Uses 'EventCode' instead of 'EventID', and 'Logon_Type'
#      instead of 'LogonType' per standard Splunk Windows TA (Splunk_TA_windows).
#    - Status Codes: Splunk indexers may normalize hex to uppercase or lowercase;
#      both casing variants ('0xc000006d' OR '0xC000006D') are matched.
#    - Sliding vs Tumbling: streamstats provides a true sliding window identical
#      to Sigma temporal logic, unlike 'bin _time span=5m' which creates fixed blocks.
#
# 4. Fields Assumed Present:
#    - TargetUserName (Account name)
#    - IpAddress or src_ip (Network source)
#    - WorkstationName (Source host)
#    - Computer (Target system)
#
# 5. Operational & Performance Limitations:
#    - streamstats requires in-memory state tracking for active combinations of
#      (TargetUserName, IpAddress, Computer). In high-throughput enterprise
#      environments, consider bounding with 'earliest=-15m latest=now'.
# ==============================================================================

index=security sourcetype="WinEventLog:Security" EventCode=4625 Logon_Type=3
    (Status="0xc000006d" OR Status="0xC000006D")
    (SubStatus="0xc000006a" OR SubStatus="0xC000006A")
    NOT TargetUserName="*$"
| streamstats time_window=5m count as failure_count by TargetUserName, IpAddress, Computer
| where failure_count >= 5
| fields _time, TargetUserName, IpAddress, WorkstationName, Computer, failure_count, Status, SubStatus
